    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.jump2d\n\n### Description\n\nOriginally it was not made callable in a hope to be more straightforward to use in mappings: no need to generate options on every mapping use and no need to pre-define option tables in config.\r\n\r\nThere are at least two downsides to this approach:\r\n- It makes some options not configurable (see #354).\r\n- It is not aligned with other modules using `gen_*` approach.",
